WEBVTT

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.620
<i>Monsters threaten human life.</i>

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.690
<i>They are opposed by brave adventurers!</i>

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:14.520
And I, Alvin, am one of them!

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.270
Now in a party with Carla, the healer,

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.380
my journey continues!

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
My Healer!

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.760
<b>So, this is Part 2 of the "What Story Is This?" arc...</b>

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.590
C'mon, open it! At least try?

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:01.290
This is... a treasure chest, right?

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:02.560
Yeah.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.780
But I never thought I would find 
myself mocked by a treasure chest.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.770
C'mon, open it! At least try?

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:09.760
Or maybe mocked by a sign?

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.440
I think it's quite amazing.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.470
It means you're an exceptional person.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.410
It's extremely upsetting.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:18.180
Who'd leave a treasure chest 
in the middle of the road?

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.140
It's too strange.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.510
It's definitely strange.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:23.970
Well, should we open it?

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.050
Ah, the strangeness is coming 
from inside the house.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:28.160
You don't want to open it?

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.430
We are still adventurers, 
crumble though we are.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.880
We really should open it!

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.380
I think you meant "humble" there.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.820
And you'd have to be stupid to open 
something that obviously fishy...

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.340
About as stupid as you are, I guess.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.280
C-Cruelzo!

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:46.020
Did you just call me stupid?

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.040
Wait, maybe he said "student" 
and I just misheard.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.300
Did you call me a stude—

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.690
I said stupid.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.560
You said stupid?

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.700
No getting around that one, I'm afraid.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:03.200
And by "stupid" you didn't mean 
"stupid cute" or something like that?

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.840
Like a puppy?

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:05.560
No.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:06.800
Come on, <i>try</i> to mean that!

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:07.730
I refuse!

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.190
I'm begging you!

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:10.970
Stop it! What are you doing?!

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:13.070
Don't pull it! Let go!

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.670
Hey, you two.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.210
What?

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.060
I just checked it with my thief skills,

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.620
and there are no traps of any 
kind on the treasure chest.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:21.970
What?

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.680
But it's such an obvious trap!

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.900
Maybe they gave it the trap-like 
trappings to keep people away?

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:33.230
I can't say for sure, but there 
might be a real treasure in there!

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.360
There's no way...

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.840
But I guess it's not impossible.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.480
And if the chest is there, 
we might as well try.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.060
Open it! Open it! Open it!

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:47.740
<b>Open it! Scrub-brush!</b>

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:47.740
Scrub-brush! Scrub-brush! Scrub-brush!

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.750
Stop egging me on!

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:52.010
If there aren't any traps, 
I might as well open it...

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:56.530
But it'll probably be a prank, or a 
sign reading "Sorry! No treasure!"

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.680
Yeah, probably.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.500
Scrub-brush.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.490
Oh, wait a minute!

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:04.800
Although there are no traps 
on the chest itself—

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:11.750
I was about to say, there are frequently 
traps <i>around</i> a treasure chest,

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.260
so you should be careful...

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.120
But I guess I was too late.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.130
Alvin-san's special talent.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.530
The hole-in-one.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.540
A-A-Are you all right?

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.210
Yeah.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.070
Were you hurt?

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:32.620
Yeah.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.540
You don't seem bothered in the slightest!

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:37.080
Can you get out?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.330
Hang on. Let's see.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:42.350
I guess not.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:45.350
I was just thinking...

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:46.300
What is it?

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:54.440
m 0 0 l 211 0 l 211 75 l 0 75

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:54.440
1 Mushroom 1 Person on a side-quest\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.880
Altargaia is knowledgeable about medicinal 
herbs and other plants, right?

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.040
These are good for diarrhea.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.110
My!

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.110
We really picked a lot!

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.730
Ryoko-san has incredible storage skills.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.830
I have a fair amount of thief skills.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:05.510
Yeah.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.600
Carla-chan is a holy woman.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.460
There's room for debate on that one!

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.480
Objection!

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.340
Quiet, you!

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:16.450
In other words, we all have our 
personal skills and specialties.

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:17.480
Can we not go here?

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:18.790
But you, quite frankly—

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.210
Anna-san!

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.190
Please don't say that.

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:24.680
Could you not dust yourself off right there?

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:28.050
A person's worth isn't decided by 
how useful or useless they are.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.820
<i>And</i> you're standing on my mantle.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:34.420
Besides, Alvin-san has a lot of good points!

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:36.240
Let's hear them!

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:39.700
Well, you know... the things!

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.040
You don't know.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.520
I do so!

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:46.750
You just have so many good points, 
I can't figure out where to start!

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:49.650
In one moment's thought, 
I came up with 200 million!

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.530
Liar. You haven't thought of a single—

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:52.900
Wait, 200 million?!

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.690
That's the number children 
use when they're lying!

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.050
At least say a hundred!

00:05:57.050 --> 00:06:00.260
A hundred good points? 
Don't you think highly of yourself!

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.120
Yeah, right!

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.920
Whatever. You're trying to say 
I don't have any good points.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:08.640
That's not true!

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:10.000
Here's one!

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.260
Those tin plates you're always wearing

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.840
are great for grilling meat!

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:15.230
What are you talking about?

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:17.380
And that doesn't even 
qualify as a good point!

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:18.590
Number two!

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:19.510
No one asked!

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.560
You've got nothing!

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:24.740
Here's one!

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:26.930
You can also grill fish!

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.080
In other words, nothing!

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:30.150
Carla-chan, Carla-chan.

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:31.710
Don't forget...

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.080
Oh, that's right.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.450
I forgot something very important!

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.450
First, you need to add oil!

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:39.490
It'll burn if you don't.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:40.950
I don't care how you do it!

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:45.000
Why are you talking about 
using my armor to cook?!

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.850
You're supposed to be talking 
about <i>my</i> good points!

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:49.830
At least say I'm nice or something!

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:52.600
Y-You can cook rice, too?!

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.400
The wonders of civilization!

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.920
Just rip my ears off!

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:16.870
Don't push yourself too hard!

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.880
What exactly are you doing?

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:21.130
Well? Can you get out now?

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:22.630
Why would you even think that?

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.370
Very strange...

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.900
Talking about yourself, now?

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:28.130
The moment I said, "Pah!"

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.100
I thought you'd "vwoop" out of the hole

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.340
Boop!

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.700
and land like "boop!"

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.040
It wasn't a dream!

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:36.930
But I guess I can't do it 
like the professionals do.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.550
Whew, that was hard work!

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:40.130
The professionals?

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:42.430
You don't know it? The famous ones!

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.680
I seriously have no idea 
what you're talking about!

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:48.530
Come on! Carla-chan is working 
very hard to try and save you!

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:50.570
You need to put in the work, too!

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.350
Come on, I'm stuck in here and can't get—

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.400
Hey, I'm more mobile than I thought I was!

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.360
See?

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:58.200
Sorry...

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.530
I might just be able to pull myself out!

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:03.050
Wait one minute.

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:05.660
I'm going to try and save you.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:08.040
Per-so-nall-y!

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.120
Seriously, it's fine.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.500
I can probably get myself out.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.410
No, pushing yourself is forbidden.

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:13.670
Seriously, it's fine!

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:15.420
Please, accept my offer.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:18.390
If you're not careful, 
you might tear yourself in half.

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.730
Just leave this to me.

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:22.080
I won't tear myself in half! I'm fine!

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.300
No, there's a roughly 90% 
chance that you will.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:26.040
Let her do it!

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:28.790
I think Carla-chan really wants to help you!

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:30.630
What a freaking pain!

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.570
Fine.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.880
All right, Carla, help me out.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:38.180
I-Indeed I shall!

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:42.400
Carla-chan?

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:47.260
<i>I know I typically annoy him, 
but we've been through so much...</i>

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.840
<i>Enough to suggest that I'm going to 
</i>keep<i> annoying him in the future,</i>

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.120
<i>but he'll tolerate it better 
if I get on his good side now!</i>

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.530
All right, time is money, people!

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.880
We'll start from the part 
where you ask me for help—

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.890
Up I go.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:01.000
Boy, I'm all dirty.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.890
I better find somewhere to wash off.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.640
Are you just playing with my feelings?!

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:08.580
It was pretty obvious you 
were plotting against me.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:12.640
Monster! Beast! Devil! Cultist! 
Lord of Darkness! Emperor of Darkness!

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:15.730
River demon! Force of darkness! 
Holy warrior of light!

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:14.390
H-Hang on...

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:17.950
Hey, you mixed a nice one in there!

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:18.860
So many appropriate titles, 
I don't know where to start!

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:21.660
It's a night parade of shame!

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:21.660
What?!

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.420
Now, then...

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:26.910
You aren't going to open it?

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:30.170
We know there are no traps 
on the chest itself.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.250
You really should just open it already.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.600
How long are you going to drag this out?

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:37.310
But there are definitely 
traps around it, right?

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:41.540
In other words, someone put the 
chest here for malicious purposes.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:45.180
That makes it an obvious prank. 
No need to open it at all.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:46.700
He's chickening out.

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:50.180
You're embarrassed about falling 
for that cheap, little trap,

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:52.300
so you want to get out of 
here ASAP. I understand.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.310
Can you not bring it up again?

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:56.120
It's all right.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:59.670
It appears our bold front-liner 
is chickening out.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.090
Very well.

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:03.120
I'll open it instead.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.720
The giant chicken can just stand back there.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:09.230
My hopes aren't particularly high,

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:11.160
but come demon, come serpent...

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:13.160
come snake...

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.170
come viper...

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:18.410
Actually, what if it's a <i>really</i> big snake?

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:21.550
Ka-boom!

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.240
Wh-Wh-What are you doing?!

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:25.640
Sorry, I couldn't help it.

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.560
Don't shout at people like that!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.750
I'm really sorry!

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:29.950
You'll pay for this!

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:30.560
Unforgivable!

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:32.310
Sue-the-pants-off-you Stance!

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:35.000
She's revealed it! 
That ancient martial arts stance!

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.260
I'll ruin you! I'll see you in court!

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:46.940
Who are you again?

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:48.690
Who am I again?

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.020
I'm a mimic.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:51.160
I was in there!

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:52.130
In there?

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:56.960
Now, look at what you've done!

00:10:57.700 --> 00:10:58.720
What?

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.960
I've been waiting in there for three days.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.910
And now it's all for nothing!

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:05.520
I really didn't mean any harm!

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.260
The poor little guy! You're so mean!

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:10.010
Mayor Mean of Mean City.

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:14.220
First, you wasted so much time falling 
into that stupid, little pit trap!

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.270
I was supposed to be the main event here!

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:18.440
But she said there were no traps!

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:23.150
Really scaring you guys could've 
been my ticket to a promotion!

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:26.160
My trap detection skill 
doesn't pick up mimics!

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:28.610
I'm getting a pay cut for this for sure!

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:31.450
Anna-san, he's still just a beginner.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:33.160
You heard that?

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.820
I'm sorry about our little fool.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:40.810
He's still learning. Please forgive him.

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:45.210
But he is an excellent 
cooking appliance, so...

00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:47.810
Not sure how that's supposed 
to make him feel better.

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.630
Besides, I think you've just 
misunderstood something.

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:53.560
That was just a rehearsal.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:55.810
A rehearsal?

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:57.840
Of course!

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:01.820
Even the world's best dancer can't go 
from zero to the stage in one night!

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:04.960
A professional performance 
demands a rehearsal!

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:06.270
That's true!

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:09.040
Yeah, I thought something felt off there!

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.580
Of course! It's a rehearsal!

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.940
So you were testing how 
well my pit trap worked!

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:14.920
Of course!

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:19.740
I didn't <i>think</i> anybody would be stupid 
enough to fall into that silly little trap!

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:20.720
Of course!

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:24.480
No one except for an adventurer 
with beginner level 100!

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.470
C'mon, open it! At least try?

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:28.740
Does that mean this is the real performance?

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:29.380
Yes!

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:30.320
Great!

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:32.890
I'm <i>really</i> gonna scare you this time!

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:36.770
And I'm going to be more 
scared than ever before!

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:39.420
I can't wait!

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:40.730
Can we get this over with?

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:42.700
I'm counting on you!

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:45.600
You got it backwards!

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.360
Okay!

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:52.030
We'll start from Carla-chan 
opening the treasure chest!

00:12:52.030 --> 00:12:54.330
Six seconds to roll!

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:57.410
Five, four, three...

00:12:56.260 --> 00:13:00.620
My goodness! I've stumbled 
upon a random treasure chest!

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.070
Huh? What?

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:04.760
I don't think she understands 
what a countdown is.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.380
What luck!

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:09.060
It must be good karma!

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:11.750
I should really get to opening it!

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:13.490
I'm opening it now!

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:15.960
I'm opening up on the count of three!

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.040
On the count of three, right?

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:19.150
Okay...

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:19.770
Ten!

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:21.250
She's starting from 10?

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.890
Nine! Wait a minute...

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:24.650
What if there's a mimic in this chest?

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:26.170
Sh-She's sharp!

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:27.410
Does she know I'm in here?

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:30.330
That could really be trouble.

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:33.030
I've heard that mimics are 
very frightening monsters!

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:37.030
That their true form is that 
of a nightmare turned flesh!

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:39.560
Six arms, eight legs...

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:42.670
Countless tentacles sprouting 
from their heads!

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.920
They're surely nothing like the 
monsters you see in picture books,

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:51.040
childish, little monsters with a 
single eye and small horns...

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:54.300
There's no way a real mimic 
could be something that silly.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:57.980
And even if they were, that would simply 
be a disguise to get our guard down.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:01.180
Surely, deep down, 
they are truly terrifying monsters!

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:07.950
When it really counts, they'll manifest 
the most terrifying visage imaginable!

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:12.620
Just imagining it has me trembling in fear!

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:17.090
However! As an adventurer, I cannot 
refuse the treasure chest's call!

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.090
No matter what horrifying 
creature waits within!

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:23.690
Pray for me!

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.290
It's locked.

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.630
Much like your heart.

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:44.560
I think there's a fracture.

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:46.600
It might even be broken!

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:48.560
It's really swelling!

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:49.800
Does it hurt?

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:53.250
The pain-relieving herbs are doing their 
thing, so I feel fine for now, but...

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:57.950
But it's lucky you weren't 
hurt worse than that.

00:14:57.950 --> 00:14:59.740
Yeah, that was pretty scary.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:02.690
Never thought we'd run into a cyclops!

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:05.250
And...

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:07.550
That she'd be changing when we did.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.320
She really got me hard out of nowhere.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.450
I'm lucky it wasn't worse, but...

00:15:21.450 --> 00:15:24.890
No young girl likes to be walked 
in on while she's changing!

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:27.350
I was more surprised that 
she was a young girl!

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:31.220
Still, Carla really saved me this time.

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:34.370
True, you'd have been in real 
trouble if not for Carla-chan.

00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:37.750
I r-really didn't do anything...

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:40.040
No need to be modest, Carla-chan!

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.460
Really?

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:42.250
In that case...

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.380
Worship me!

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.640
Stow it!

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:47.860
But thanks to Carla...

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:49.390
Are you all right?

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:52.260
That was close. Even the 
glancing blow hurts like hell.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:55.690
Anyway, for now we should run—

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:57.250
Hey, Carla!

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:59.140
I b-beg your pardon!

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.900
Stupid! Get away!

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:03.520
Carla! What in the world are you—

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:06.520
That lingerie! Is that from 
the new spring collection?!

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.280
What is she talking about?

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:11.510
Look at that face! She's totally baffled!

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:12.990
Wow, you recognize it?!

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:14.290
She understands?!

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:16.050
I sure do!

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:19.410
That capital city brand, 
"Scent of a Dwarf," right?

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.920
You've got great taste!

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:23.350
Wow, you can tell?

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:24.540
You're so right!

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:28.280
I'm on my way to fight a 
nearby village's garrison!

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:31.060
I see! They're your go-for-it panties, then?

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:33.390
Yes, pink for spring!

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:34.260
Okay, the boys wait over there!

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:34.470
Charming, aren't they?

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.140
This is girl-talk time!

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:35.310
They look great on you!

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:39.000
Is that what "go-for-it panties" means?

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:44.030
Thanks to Carla distracting 
her, nothing happened.

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:46.840
Yes, nothing happened at all...

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.440
No heart-racing, pulse-pounding battle...

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:53.200
Of course... it's always best to 
avoid conflict if you can, but...

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:57.280
I'm sorry I'm more talented 
than a certain front-liner.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:16:58.600
Knock it off.

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:01.200
But what happened with that monster, anyway?

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:04.340
We exchanged contact information.

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:06.960
Let's go shopping some time!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:10.510
You're pretty good at 
talking things out, huh?

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:13.110
At any rate, I need to heal you!

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:13.970
R-Right.

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:17.610
Hey, are you going to use 
proper healing magic?

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:20.840
I mean, you're a healer, so this 
shouldn't be that surprising...

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:24.010
You defended me earlier, so...

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:26.340
But forget that. Healing comes first.

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:28.860
S-Sure. Get to it.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:43.370
Bwaaaaaa!

00:17:41.550 --> 00:17:42.940
Shut up!

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:45.920
Hey! Do you really have to yell that loud?!

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:50.080
Son of a bitch!

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:50.080
Wait! Hold on a minute!

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.150
And stop shouting!

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:52.780
Stop it!

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:53.500
Fwakyuu!

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:55.760
Knock it off!

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:56.890
What's wrong with you?

00:17:56.890 --> 00:18:00.880
Could you please not stop me 
in the middle of healing you?

00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:02.040
Harrumph!

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:03.230
I had to stop you!

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:06.590
If your "chant" involves screaming 
names at me, I'm going to stop you!

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:08.150
And what was "Fwakyuu" thing?

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:11.070
Very well. I'll do it properly.

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:13.010
Then what was that last one?!

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:15.400
Ryoko-san, could you fetch me a cloth?

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:18.900
Certainly, Carla-san.

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:24.040
Is Ryoko-san just our bag of holding now?

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:27.360
Ryoko-san has a very 
high-level storage skill!

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:29.130
I appreciate that!

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:32.030
Is "storage" what this really is?

00:18:32.030 --> 00:18:34.330
So, what are you going 
to do with that cloth?

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:36.240
Well, just watch.

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:38.180
It's a completely ordinary cloth.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:40.040
If I place it over your arm...

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:44.180
I'll infuse it with power, 
then remove it on the count of three.

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:46.050
Looks pretty much like 
what you did last time.

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:48.060
One, two...

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:50.320
She really doesn't understand 
the concept of a countdown.

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:51.470
What?!

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:52.930
The swelling's gone?

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:55.620
And it almost seems kind of shiny now...

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:57.560
It was sleight-of-hand?!

00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:59.070
It was hand power!

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:01.120
Incredible, I guess!

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:09.340
It really was pretty surprising, though...

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:11.600
What are you talking about now?

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:15.090
I just can't believe you can 
use normal healing magic.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:17.970
Though I guess that wasn't 
exactly "normal," anyway...

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:22.240
Are you saying you thought I 
couldn't use real magic before?!

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:24.440
Well, given your history and all.

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:28.620
You mean you thought I was 
merely a beautiful girl

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:31.220
overflowing with motherly instinct, 
intelligence, and love?

00:19:31.220 --> 00:19:32.300
You flatter me.

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:33.180
I didn't think that.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:36.820
Though, to be honest... 
you are pretty amazing.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:40.400
You seem to have powerful magical skills,

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:41.820
despite the whole "personality" thing...

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:43.900
There you are!

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:47.110
But a guy my age still 
doesn't have any stars,

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:50.350
and other adventurers still 
call me the "veteran rookie."

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:55.710
Lately, I've been thinking that a weirdo 
like you might be a good match for me.

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:57.380
Over there!

00:19:56.710 --> 00:20:01.160
If you were more normal, you'd probably 
be part of a different party,

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.630
and I'd probably still be solo.

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:05.440
Got you this time!

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:09.390
You've dealt me your share 
of psychological damage...

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:11.830
but... you know...

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:14.650
I guess I should say...

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:15.770
Thank you.

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:18.490
Let's keep working together.

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:22.280
What? Where'd she go?

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:26.670
E-Enough of those fully 
justified words of gratitude!

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:33.160
B-Besides, I-I'm the bun choose 
happy... joined a party...

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:35.670
w-w-with...

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:37.810
Just be grateful!

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:39.340
This is what I'm talking about!

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:46.800
Time to head out, I think.

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:49.320
Help me!

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:53.590
Help me!

00:20:56.380 --> 00:21:15.800
<b>I am the Dwarf mayor.
 The great sorcerer of darkness, Dorman,
 is attacking our village to try 
to steal our sacred artifact.
 If Dorman retrieves the artifact, 
the world will be destroyed.
Brave warrior, I beg of you, 
foil Dorman's plot! Please!
 I am the Dwarf mayor.</b>

00:20:58.990 --> 00:21:01.260
"The great sorcerer of darkness, Dorman,

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:04.730
is attacking our village to try 
to steal our sacred artifact.

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:08.810
If Dorman retrieves the artifact, 
the world will be destroyed."

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:15.800
"Brave warrior, I beg of you, 
foil Dorman's plot! Please!"

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:17.760
My grandpa is the mayor.

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:21.390
He told me to give that message 
to a nice-looking person.

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:26.440
He got me out, but then he got captured 
with the rest of the villagers...

00:21:26.440 --> 00:21:29.020
Please, save them all!

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:34.400
Dorman is a major bad guy who leads an 
army of magically-crafted soldiers!

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:36.030
Dorman, eh?

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:38.410
I've certainly heard of him.

00:21:38.410 --> 00:21:39.390
His magic power is five-star...

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:43.780
No, likely far greater than that.

00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:49.540
Zero-star lol-in-parentheses 
Alvin-san doesn't stand a chance.

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:25.540 --> 00:23:27.170
They called us in for the preview?!

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:28.800
This is the last episode, after all!

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:29.670
Really?

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:30.980
You didn't know?

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:32.800
We all get slain by the bad guys.

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:33.400
No way!

00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:35.140
You'll have to watch and see!

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:36.590
I really can't wait!

00:23:36.590 --> 00:23:38.790
Watch it, everyone!

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>"We've reached the final episode at last and the entire staff including
those on the manga side would like to thank you all for watching but
because the manga doesn't yet contain a story that could be used for a
final episode this is basically going to be a totally original story although we
made sure to get the dwarf character designs and lines and ideas from
the creator Hakko-sensei so we were able to make it feel consistent
but it's also sad to reach the end at last and while we'd really like to
spend more time with Carla and Alvin and the others please remember that
their adventures will continue in the manga so continue to support them
there but anyway thank you so much for watching and once more from the
bottom of our hearts we'd like to say thank you so much
and that's the deal with episode 12 (final episode)"</b>

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>See you then!</b>

00:23:38.790 --> 00:23:40.790
We've reached the—
